amma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y) γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) &gt; − γ ∗ \\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)&gt;-{\\gamma^{*}} Now say γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 , y ) &lt; γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) \\hat{\\gamma}(\\mathbf{x},y)&lt;\\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y) ; then γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) &gt; γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 , y ) ≥ ϵ − γ ∗ ≥ − γ ∗ \\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)&gt;\\hat{\\gamma}(\\mathbf{x},y)\\geq\\epsilon-{\\gamma^{*}}\\geq-{\\gamma^{*}} So in either case we have γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) &gt; − γ ∗ \\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)&gt;-{\\gamma^{*}} . If γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) ≤ γ ∗ \\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)\\leq{\\gamma^{*}} , then | γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) | ≤ γ ∗ |\\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)|\\leq{\\gamma^{*}} so f baseline ​ ( 𝐱 ~ ) = a f_{\\text{baseline}}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}})=a . Otherwise, if γ ^ ​ ( 𝐱 ~ , y ) &gt; γ ∗ ≥ 0 \\hat{\\gamma}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}},y)&gt;{\\gamma^{*}}\\geq 0 , then f baseline ​ ( 𝐱 ~ ) = g ⁡ ( 𝐱 ~ ) = y f_{\\text{baseline}}(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}})=g(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}})=y . So ∀ 𝐱 ~ ∈ ℬ ϵ ​ ( 𝐱 ) f ⁡ ( 𝐱 ~ ) = y ∨ f ⁡ ( 𝐱 ~ ) = a \\forall\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}}\\in\\mathcal{B}_{\\epsilon}(\\mathbf{x})\\quad f(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}})=y\\vee f(\\widetilde{\\mathbf{x}})=a ∎ Appendix B Experimental Setup We implement the baseline and CARL using PyTorch ( paszke_automatic_2017 ) . All training uses the Adam optimizer ( kingma_adam:_2014 ) . We preprocess images before classification by standardizing them based on the mean and standard deviation of each channel for all images in the dataset. The MNIST dataset can be obtained from http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/ and the CIFAR-10 dataset can be obtained from https://www.cs.toronto.edu/˜kriz/cifar.html . B.1 Network Architectures For MNIST, we use train a 6-layer CNN architecture described in Table 2 . For CIFAR-10, we train a WideResNet-28-5 ( zagoruyko_wide_2016 ) . We experimented with training a WideResNet-28-10, as was used in the original paper, but 