0}^{n-1}p_{k}. Now, to obtain a formula for the sum above, beginning with conditional probability Pr ⁡ ( X k = 1 | X k − 1 ) = ω 0 + ω 1 ​ X k − 1 \\Pr(X_{k}=1\\,|\\,X_{k-1})=\\omega_{0}+\\omega_{1}X_{k-1} , using the law of total expectation, we obtain a recursion p k \\displaystyle p_{k} = \\displaystyle= 𝔼 ⁡ { Pr ⁡ ( X k = 1 | X k − 1 ) } \\displaystyle\\mathbb{E}\\left\\{\\Pr(X_{k}=1|X_{k-1})\\right\\} = \\displaystyle= ω 0 + ω 1 ​ 𝔼 ​ ( X k − 1 ) \\displaystyle\\omega_{0}+\\omega_{1}\\mathbb{E}(X_{k-1}) = \\displaystyle= 2 ​ ω 1 ​ p k − 1 + ω 0 − ω 1 , \\displaystyle 2\\omega_{1}p_{k-1}+\\omega_{0}-\\omega_{1}, where the last line follows since 𝔼 ⁡ ( X k − 1 ) = 2 ​ p k − 1 − 1 \\mathbb{E}(X_{k-1})=2p_{k-1}-1 . Initializing with p 0 = ω 0 + ω 1 ​ x − 1 p_{0}=\\omega_{0}+\\omega_{1}x_{-1} , the solution to this linear equation is, since | 2 ​ ω 1 | &lt; 1 |2\\omega_{1}|&lt;1 , p k \\displaystyle p_{k} = ( 2 ​ ω 1 ) k ​ p 0 + [ 1 − ( 2 ​ ω 1 ) k ] ​ p ∞ \\displaystyle=(2\\omega_{1})^{k}p_{0}+\\left[1-(2\\omega_{1})^{k}\\right]p_{\\infty} where p ∞ = ( ω 0 − ω 1 ) / ( 1 − 2 ​ ω 1 ) p_{\\infty}=(\\omega_{0}-\\omega_{1})/(1-2\\omega_{1}) . Thus, 𝔼 ⁡ ( H n ) n \\displaystyle\\frac{\\mathbb{E}(H_{n})}{n} = 1 n ​ ∑ k = 0 n − 1 ( 2 ​ ω 1 ) k ​ p 0 + 1 n ​ ∑ k = 0 n − 1 [ 1 − ( 2 ​ ω 1 ) k ] ​ p ∞ \\displaystyle=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}(2\\omega_{1})^{k}p_{0}+\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\left[1-(2\\omega_{1})^{k}\\right]p_{\\infty} = λ n ​ p 0 + ( 1 − λ n ) ​ p ∞ . □ \\displaystyle=\\lambda_{n}p_{0}+(1-\\lambda_{n})p_{\\infty}.\\;\\;\\square VI Deeper Memory We consider the general case of memory depth m &gt; 1 m&gt;1 and show how analytic expressions for 𝔼 ⁡ ( H n ) \\mathbb{E}(H_{n}) can be efficiently obtained. Indeed, beginning with parameterization of the conditional probability of heads Pr ⁡ ( X k = 1 | X k − 1 , X k − 2 , … , X k − m ) = ω 0 + ∑ i = 1 m ω i ​ X k − i \\Pr(X_{k}=1|X_{k-1},X_{k-2},...,X_{k-m})=\\omega_{0}+\\sum_{i=1}^{m}\\omega_{i}X_{k-i} wit