rove useful in future research, we consider a standard state-space realization of the “delay system” to represent the scalar recursion for p k p_{k} . That is, by introducing the m m -dimensional state vector which is given by v k = [ p k − m + 1 , p k − m + 2 , … , p k ] T v_{k}=[p_{k-m+1},p_{k-m+2},\\ldots,p_{k}]^{T} , we readily obtain a classical companion form realization v k + 1 = A ​ v k + b ​ u k v_{k+1}=Av_{k}+bu_{k} with triple ( A , b , c ) (A,b,c) , input u ⁡ ( k ) ≡ 1 u(k)\\equiv 1 and output being p k p_{k} . To illustrate, for memory depth m = 3 m=3 , we obtain A = [ 0 1 0 0 0 1 2 ​ ω 3 2 ​ ω 2 2 ​ ω 1 ] ; b = [ 0 0 ω 0 − ω 1 − ω 2 − ω 3 ] ; A=\\left[\\begin{array}[]{ccc}0&amp;1&amp;0\\\\ 0&amp;0&amp;1\\\\ 2\\omega_{3}&amp;2\\omega_{2}&amp;2\\omega_{1}\\\\ \\end{array}\\right];\\;\\;b=\\left[\\begin{array}[]{c}0\\\\ 0\\\\ \\omega_{0}-\\omega_{1}-\\omega_{2}-\\omega_{3}\\\\ \\end{array}\\right]; and c = [ 0 0 1 ] c=[0\\;0\\;1] with solution of the recursion given by p k \\displaystyle p_{k} = c ⁡ ( A k ​ v 0 + ∑ i = 0 k − 1 A k − 1 − i ​ b ) \\displaystyle=c\\left(A^{k}v_{0}+\\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}A^{k-1-i}b\\right) = c ⁡ ( A k ​ v 0 + ( I − A ) − 1 ​ ( I − A k ) ​ b ) \\displaystyle=c\\left(A^{k}v_{0}+(I-A)^{-1}(I-A^{k})b\\right) and the matrix I − A I-A is guaranteed to be invertible since det ​ ( I − A ) = 1 − 2 ​ ∑ i = 1 m ω i \\text{det}(I-A)=1-2\\sum_{i=1}^{m}\\omega_{i} must be non-zero due to the hyperdiamond constraint on the ω i \\omega_{i} . In addition, from Gerschgorin’s circle theorem [ 21 ] and the hyperdiamond constraint, each eigenvalue of A A has magnitude less than 1, and so A k → 0 A^{k}\\rightarrow 0 as k → ∞ k\\rightarrow\\infty . Using this fact, beginning with p k p_{k} above, this leads to the generalization of our steady-state unconditional probability p ∞ = c ​ ( I − A ) − 1 ​ b . p_{\\infty}=c(I-A)^{-1}b. Now recognizing that this corresponds to the transfer function H ⁡ ( z ) H(z) for the triple ( A , b , c ) (A,b,c) evaluated at