nd Geoffrey E Hinton. Imagenet classification with deep convolutional neural networks. In Advances in neural information processing systems , pages 1097–1105, 2012. (19) Peng Lei and Sinisa Todorovic. Temporal deformable residual networks for action segmentation in videos. 2018 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition , pages 6742–6751, 2018. (20) J. Liu, P. Carr, R. T. Collins, and Y. Liu. Tracking sports players with context-conditioned motion models. In 2013 IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition , pages 1830–1837, June 2013. (21) William McNally, Kanav Vats, Tyler Pinto, Chris Dulhanty, John McPhee, and Alexander Wong. Golfdb: A video database for golf swing sequencing. In Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops , pages 0–0, 2019. (22) Nazanin Mehrasa, Yatao Zhong, Frederick Tung, Luke Bornn, and Greg Mori. Deep learning of player trajectory representations for team activity analysis. In 11th MIT Sloan Sports Analytics Conference , 2018. (23) Alejandro Newell, Kaiyu Yang, and Jia Deng. Stacked hourglass networks for human pose estimation. In European conference on computer vision , pages 483–499. Springer, 2016. (24) AJ Piergiovanni and Michael S. Ryoo. Early detection of injuries in mlb pitchers from video. In The IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) Workshops , June 2019. (25) Alexander Richard, Hildegard Kuehne, and Juergen Gall. Weakly supervised action learning with rnn based fine-to-coarse modeling. 2017 IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) , pages 1273–1282, 2017. (26) M. Sandler, A. Howard, M. Zhu, A. Zhmoginov, and L. Chen. Mobilenetv2: Inverted residuals and linear bottlenecks. In 2018 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition , pages 4510–4520, June 2018. (27) R. A. Sharma, B. Bhat, V. Gandhi, and C. V. Jawahar. Automated top view registration of broadcast football videos. In 2018 IEEE