eters which represent, for both positive and negative streams, the reward processing weights (biases), as well as discount factors for the past rewards: λ + \\lambda_{+} and λ − \\lambda_{-} are the discount factors applied to the previously accumulated positive and negative rewards, respectively, while w + w_{+} and w − w_{-} represent the weights on the positive and negative rewards at the current iteration. We assume that at each step, an agent receives both positive and negative rewards, denote r + r^{+} and r − r^{-} , respectively (either one of them can be zero, of course). As in HBTS, the two streams are independently updated. Algorithm 2 Split CB: Split Contextual Thompson Sampling (SCTS) 1: Initialize: B a ′ + = B a ′ − = I d B_{a^{\\prime}}^{+}=B_{a^{\\prime}}^{-}=I_{d} , μ a ′ + ^ = μ a ′ − ^ = 0 d , f a ′ − = f a ′ − = 0 d , ∀ a ′ ∈ A \\hat{\\mu_{a^{\\prime}}^{+}}=\\hat{\\mu_{a^{\\prime}}^{-}}=0_{d},f_{a^{\\prime}}^{-}=f_{a^{\\prime}}^{-}=0_{d},\\forall a^{\\prime}\\in A . 2: For each episode e e do 3: Initialize state s s 4: Repeat for each step t t of the episode e e 5: Receive context x t x_{t} 6: Sample μ ~ a ′ + ∼ N ⁡ ( μ a ′ + ^ , v 2 ​ B a ′ + − 1 ) \\tilde{\\mu}^{+}_{a^{\\prime}}\\sim N(\\hat{\\mu^{+}_{a^{\\prime}}},v^{2}{B^{+}_{a^{\\prime}}}^{-1}) and μ ~ a ′ − ∼ N ⁡ ( μ a ′ − ^ , v 2 ​ B a ′ − − 1 ) , ∀ a ′ ∈ A t \\tilde{\\mu}^{-}_{a^{\\prime}}\\sim N(\\hat{\\mu^{-}_{a^{\\prime}}},v^{2}{B^{-}_{a^{\\prime}}}^{-1}),\\forall a^{\\prime}\\in A_{t} 7: Take action a = arg ⁡ max a ′ ⁡ ( x t ⊤ ​ μ ~ a ′ + + x t ⊤ ​ μ ~ a ′ − ) a=\\arg\\max_{a^{\\prime}}(x_{t}^{\\top}\\tilde{\\mu}^{+}_{a^{\\prime}}+x_{t}^{\\top}\\tilde{\\mu}^{-}_{a^{\\prime}}) , and 8: Observe r + ​ and ​ r − ∈ R a ′ r^{+}\\text{ and }r^{-}\\in R_{a^{\\prime}} 9: B a + := λ + ​ B a + + x t ​ x t ⊤ B^{+}_{a}:=\\lambda_{+}B^{+}_{a}+x_{t}x_{t}^{\\top} , f a + := λ + ​ f a + + w + ​ x t ​ r + f^{+}_{a}:=\\lambda_{+}f^{+}_{a}+w_{+}x_{t}r^{+} , μ a + ^ := B a + − 1 ​ f a + \\hat{\\mu^{+}_{a}