 discretization is particularly useful because it lumps together all the points. Data is taken from ten consecutive seasons starting 2009/10 which were retrieved from Football-data.co.uk 2019 ( EPL ) and from Pro Football reference 2021 ( NFL ). The first five “training” seasons 2009/10 – 2013/14 form 𝒮 train \\mathcal{S}_{\\textrm{train}} while the last five seasons, 2014/15 – 2018/19, are gathered in the testing set 𝒮 test \\mathcal{S}_{\\textrm{test}} and will be used to evaluate the algorithms; the same approach was adopted in Arntzen and Hvattum 2021 . The training is thus based on the results of 5 ⋅ 380 = 1900 5\\cdot 380=1900 games for the EPL and of 5 ⋅ 256 = 1280 5\\cdot 256=1280 games for the NFL . We study the model ( 3 )-( 7 ), for three different values of thresholds Δ \\Delta and also consider its generalization to J + 1 = 7 J+1=7 discretization categories defined as { d t &lt; − Δ ′′ } \\{d_{t}&lt;-\\Delta^{\\prime\\prime}\\} , { − Δ ′′ ≤ d t &lt; − Δ ′ } \\{-\\Delta^{\\prime\\prime}\\leq d_{t}&lt;-\\Delta^{\\prime}\\} , { − Δ ′ ≤ d t &lt; 0 } \\{-\\Delta^{\\prime}\\leq d_{t}&lt;0\\} , { d t = 0 } \\{d_{t}=0\\} , { 0 &lt; d t ≤ Δ ′ } \\{0&lt;d_{t}\\leq\\Delta^{\\prime}\\} , { Δ ′ &lt; d t ≤ − Δ ′′ } \\{\\Delta^{\\prime}&lt;d_{t}\\leq-\\Delta^{\\prime\\prime}\\} , and { Δ ′′ &lt; d t } \\{\\Delta^{\\prime\\prime}&lt;d_{t}\\} , indexed, respectively by y t = 0 , … , 6 y_{t}=0,\\ldots,6 . Although we ensured that the values f h f_{h} are far from zero, see Table 1 , no formal criterion was used to find the thresholds as our goal was rather to illustrate the flexibility of the proposed algorithm. For the EPL we use Δ ∈ { 1 , 2 , 3 } \\Delta\\in\\{1,2,3\\} (when J + 1 = 5 J+1=5 ) as well as Δ ′ = 1 \\Delta^{\\prime}=1 and Δ ′′ = 2 \\Delta^{\\prime\\prime}=2 ( J + 1 = 7 J+1=7 ). For the NFL the difference in the scores are larger than in association football and we use Δ ∈ { 5 , 10 , 15 } \\Delta\\in\\{5,10,15\\} ( J + 1 − 5 J+1-5 ) and Δ ′ = 5 \\Delta^{\\p