-sale constrained Merton problem) . In the limiting case when q q = = 0 0 , the drawdown constraint is reduced to a non-negativity constraint on the wealth process, and by Lemma 3.3 , this means a no-short selling and no borrowing constraint on the portfolio strategies. When the drift B B is also known, equal to b 0 b_{0} , and for a CRRA utility function, let us then consider the corresponding constrained Merton problem with value function denoted by v k M v_{k}^{M} , k k = = 0 , … , N 0,\\ldots,N , which satisfies the standard backward recursion from dynamic programming: { v N M ​ ( x ) = x p p , x &gt; 0 , v k M ​ ( x ) = sup a ′ ​ 𝟙 d ≤ 1 a ∈ [ 0 , 1 ] d 𝔼 [ v k + 1 M ( x ( 1 + a ′ ( e b 0 + ϵ k + 1 − 𝟙 d ) ) ] , k = 0 , … , N − 1 . \\displaystyle\\left\\{\\begin{aligned} v_{N}^{M}(x)&amp;=\\frac{x^{p}}{p},\\;\\;x&gt;0,\\\\ v_{k}^{M}(x)&amp;=\\displaystyle\\sup_{\\begin{subarray}{c}a^{\\prime}\\mathbbm{1}_{d}\\leq 1\\\\ a\\in[0,1]^{d}\\end{subarray}}\\mathbb{E}\\Big[v_{k+1}^{M}\\big(x\\big(1+a^{\\prime}\\big(e^{b_{0}+\\epsilon_{k+1}}-\\mathbbm{1}_{d}\\big)\\big)\\Big],\\quad k=0,\\ldots,N-1.\\end{aligned}\\right. (20) Searching for a solution of the form v k M ​ ( x ) v_{k}^{M}(x) = = K k ​ x p / p K_{k}x^{p}/p , with K k ≥ 0 K_{k}\\geq 0 for all k ∈ [ [ 0 , N ] ] k\\in[\\![0,N]\\!] , we see that the sequence ( K k ) k (K_{k})_{k} satisfies the recursive relation: K k \\displaystyle K_{k} = \\displaystyle= S ​ K k + 1 , k = 0 , … , N − 1 , \\displaystyle SK_{k+1},\\quad k=0,\\ldots,N-1, starting from K N K_{N} = = 1 1 , where S \\displaystyle S : ⁣ = \\displaystyle:= sup a ′ ​ 𝟙 d ≤ 1 a ∈ [ 0 , 1 ] d 𝔼 ⁡ [ ( 1 + a ′ ​ ( e b 0 + ϵ 1 − 𝟙 d ) ) p ] , \\displaystyle\\displaystyle\\sup_{\\begin{subarray}{c}a^{\\prime}\\mathbbm{1}_{d}\\leq 1\\\\ a\\in[0,1]^{d}\\end{subarray}}\\mathbb{E}\\Big[\\Big(1+a^{\\prime}\\big(e^{b_{0}+\\epsilon_{1}}-\\mathbbm{1}_{d}\\big)\\Big)^{p}\\Big], by recalling that ϵ 1 \\epsilon_{1} , … \\dots , ϵ N \\epsilon_{N} are i.i.d. random varia