ffects of\n                                                                        also useful for the model as it further gives around a 2%\nthe pressure built on the batsman when the number of\n                                                                        average boost to the model.\nwickets fallen are more.\n     The experiments conducted with the above four model\n                                                                                  Table IV: Improved Performance Results\nvariants are shown in the experiments section below.\n                                                                                   Model                  Test Accuracy (%)\n            IV. EXPERIMENTS AND ABLATION STUDY\n                                                                                                          J=300     J=250      J=200\nA. Performance Comparison of the Model Variants:\n     The four model variants are compared in this section.                         Baseline                95.7      75.1      66.4\nTable II. reports the test accuracy in % on the ODIs dataset.\nModels A,B,C and D are as explained in the section above.               Augmenting Pre-match results       96.3      77.6      68.2\n“J” is the number of balls bowled till then. So in short, the            Augmenting Target Scores          98.0      90.1      87.1\ntable gives the accuracy of the predictions of the model after\nthe Jth ball.                                                               Augmenting Wickets             98.4      92.5      88.2\n                 Table II. Model Comparison\n        Model                   Test Accuracy (%)\n                                                                        D. Best Model and its performance with overs\n                         J=300         J=250          J=200                  We experiment on four different model variants and\n      Model A             93.7          63.5           57.2             select the b