ed\nhorse races.\nMaster’s thesis, Department of Computer Science, University of\nBristol.\nSuhonen et al.,  (2018)\nSuhonen, N., Saastamoinen, J., Kainulainen, T., and Forrest, D. (2018).\nIs timing everything in horse betting?\nEconomics Letters\n, 173:97–99.\nSung et al.,  (2016)\nSung, M., Johnson, J., and McDonald, D. (2016).\nInformed trading, market efficiency, and volatility.\nEconomics Letters\n, 149:65–59.\nSwidler and Shaw,  (1995)\nSwidler, S. and Shaw, R. (1995).\nRacetrack wagering and the “uninformed” bettor: A study of market\nefficiency.\nQuarterly Review of Economics and Finance\n, 35(3):305–314.\nTeräsvirta and Zhao,  (2010)\nTeräsvirta, T. and Zhao, Z. (2010).\nStylized facts of return series, robust estimates, and three popular\nmodels of volatility.\nApplied Financial Economics\n, 21:67–94.\nTesauro and Bredin,  (2002)\nTesauro, G. and Bredin, J. (2002).\nSequential strategic bidding in auctions using dynamic programming.\nIn\nProceedings AAMAS 2002\n.\nTesauro and Das,  (2001)\nTesauro, G. and Das, R. (2001).\nHigh-performance bidding agents for the continuous double auction.\nIn\nProceedings of the 3rd ACM Conference on Electronic\nCommerce\n, pages 206–209.\nThompkins et al.,  (2008)\nThompkins, R., Ziemba, W., and Hodges, S. (2008).\nThe favourite-longshot bias in S&P500 and FTSE100 index futures\noptions: The returns to bets and the cost of insurance.\nIn Hausch, D. and Ziemba, W., editors,\nHandbook of Sports &\nLottery Markets\n, pages 161–180. North Holland.\nThorp,  (2006)\nThorp, E. (2006).\nThe Kelly Criterion in blackjack sports betting, and the stock\nmarket.\nIn Zenios, S. and Ziemba, W., editors,\nHandbook of Asset and\nLiability Management\n, volume 1, pages 385–428. Elsevier.\nThorp,  (2017)\nThorp, E. (2017).\nA Man for All Markets: Beating the Odds, from Las Vegas to Wall\nStreet\n.\nOneworld.\nTsrimpas,  (2015)\nTsrimpas, P. (2015).\nSpecification and Performance Optimization of Real-Time Trading\nStrategies for Betting Exchange Platforms\n.\nPhD thesis, Imperial College London, Department of Computing.\nTversky and Kahneman,  (1992)\nTversky, A. and Kahneman, D. (1992).\nAdvances in prospect theory: Cumulative representation of\nuncertainty.\nJournal of Risk and Uncertainty\n, 5:297–323.\nVaughan Williams,  (2003)\nVaughan Williams, L., editor (2003).\nThe Economics of Gambling\n.\nRoutledge.\nVaughan Williams,  (2009)\nVaughan Williams, L., editor (2009).\nInformation Efficiency in Financial and Betting Markets\n.\nCambridge University Press.\nVytelingum et al.,  (2008)\nVytelingum, P., Cliff, D., and Jennings, N. (2008).\nStrategic bidding in continuous double auctions.\nArtificial Intelligence\n, 172(14):1700–1729.\nWall et al.,  (2017)\nWall, M., Costello, R., and Lindsay, S. (2017).\nThe miracle of the markets: Identifying key campaign events in the\nScottish Independence Referendum using betting odds.\nElectoral Studies\n, 46:39–47.\nWheatcroft,  (2020)\nWheatcroft, E. (2020).\nA profitable model for predicting the over/under market in football.\nInternational Journal of Forecasting\n, 36:916–932.\nWilkens,  (2020)\nWilkens, S. (2020).\nSports prediction and betting models in the machine learning age: The\ncase of tennis.\nSSRN:3506302\n.\n◄\nFeeling\nlucky?\nConversion\nreport\nReport\nan issue\nView original\non arXiv\n►"}
{"id": "arxiv-sweep/fulltext/2105.10700.txt", "corpus": "arxiv-sweep", "kind": "fulltext", "chars": 3859, "equations": [], "text": "[2105.10700] Soccer Player Tracking in Low Quality Video Skip to main content Search Submit Donate Log in Search arXiv Press Enter to search &middot; Advanced search --> Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition arXiv:2105.10700 (cs) [Submitted on 22 May 2021] Title: Soccer Player Tracking in Low Quality Video Authors: Eloi Martins , José Henrique Brito View a PDF of the paper titled Soccer Player Tracking in Low Quality Video, by Eloi Martins and 1 other authors View PDF Abstract: In this paper we propose a system capable of tracking multiple soccer players in different types of video quality. The main goal, in contrast to most state-of-art soccer player tracking systems, is the ability of execute effectively tracking in videos of low-quality. We adapted a state-of-art Multiple Object Tracking to the task. In order to do that adaptation, we created a Detection and a Tracking Dataset for 3 different qualities of video. The results of our system are conclusive of its high performance. Subjects: Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV) Cite as: arXiv:2105.10700 [cs.CV] &nbsp; (or arXiv:2105.10700v1 [cs.CV] for this version) &nbsp; https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2105.10700 Focus to learn more arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite Submission history From: José Henrique Brito [ view email ] [v1] Sat, 22 May 2021 11:55:08 UTC (356 KB) Full-text links: Access Paper: View a PDF of the paper titled Soccer Player Tracking in Low Quality Video, by Eloi Martins and 1 other authors View PDF view license Current browse context: cs.CV &lt;&nbsp;prev &nbsp; | &nbsp; next&nbsp;&gt; new | recent | 2021-05 Change to browse by: cs References &amp; Citations NASA ADS Google Scholar Semantic Scholar DBLP - CS Bibliography listing | bibtex export BibTeX citation Loading... BibTeX formatted citation &times; loading... Data provided by: Bookmark