{\\mathrm{p}_{x}\\cdot t}\\right\\rangle=\\sum_{x}\\mathrm{p}_{x}\\cdot\\dfrac{a_{x}^{\\tau}+1}{\\mathrm{p}_{x}t}=\\dfrac{\\tau+M}{t} , the average discrepancy from Kelly’s estimate is asymptotically the same for a pseudo and a classical Laplace’s estimate: ⟨ log ⁡ p x − log ⁡ b x md-LAPL , t + 1 ⟩ ≈ M − 1 2 ​ t . \\left\\langle\\log\\mathrm{p}_{x}-\\log\\mathrm{b}_{x}^{\\text{\\tiny md-LAPL},~t+1}\\right\\rangle\\approx\\dfrac{M-1}{2t}. (40) This is reasonable because in the long run the information contained in the prior becomes negligible with respect to the information contained in the likelihood. Appendix C Proof of the equivalence between 𝐛 LAPL \\mathbf{b}^{\\text{\\tiny LAPL}} and 𝐛 PORTF \\mathbf{b}^{\\text{\\tiny PORTF}} Keeping in mind that: ∫ ℝ + M d ​ 𝐛 ​ δ ​ ( ∑ x ~ b x ~ − r ) ​ ∏ x ~ = 1 M b x ~ n x ~ = ∏ x ~ n x ~ ! ( ∑ x ~ n x ~ + M − 1 ) ! ​ r ∑ x ~ n x ~ + M − 1 , \\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{M}_{+}}\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{b}~\\delta\\left(\\sum_{\\tilde{x}}\\mathrm{b}_{\\tilde{x}}-r\\right)~\\prod_{\\tilde{x}=1}^{M}\\mathrm{b}_{\\tilde{x}}^{n_{\\tilde{x}}}=\\dfrac{\\prod_{\\tilde{x}}n_{\\tilde{x}}!}{(\\sum_{\\tilde{x}}n_{\\tilde{x}}+M-1)!}~r^{\\sum_{\\tilde{x}}n_{\\tilde{x}}+M-1}, (41) where r ∈ ℝ + r\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+} and ∀ x , n x ∈ ℝ + \\forall x,~n_{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}_{+} (for any real number a a , we will write a ! ≡ Γ ⁡ ( a + 1 ) a!\\equiv\\Gamma(a+1) ), we can perform an explicit computation of ( 11 ) with the assumption of Kelly’s model: ( 11 ): ∫ ℝ + M d 𝐛 δ ( ∑ x ~ b x ~ − 1 ) b x C [ 𝐛 , t | 𝐱 t ] = O ​ ∫ ℝ + M d ​ 𝐛 ​ δ ​ ( ∑ x ~ b x ~ − 1 ) ​ ∏ x ~ b x ~ n x ~ t + δ x , x ~ = O ​ ( n x t + 1 ) ! ​ ∏ x ~ ≠ x n x ~ t ! ( t + M ) ! , \\begin{split}\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{M}_{+}}\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{b}~\\delta\\left(\\sum_{\\tilde{x}}\\mathrm{b}_{\\tilde{x}}-1\\right)~\\mathrm{b}_{x}~C\\left[\\mathbf{b},t|\\mathbf{x}^{t}\\right]&amp;=O~\\int_{\\mathbb{R}^{M}_{+}}\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{b}~\\delta\\left(\\sum_{\\tilde{x}}\\mathrm{b}_{\\tilde{x}}-1\\right)~\\p