dy-state probability of winning 𝐩 s \\mathbf{p}^{\\text{s}} is well defined. Expanding the square root yields: τ y t ≈ p y s ​ t + 1 2 ​ σ y ​ w t p y s . \\sqrt{\\tau_{y}^{t}}\\approx\\sqrt{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}t}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\dfrac{\\sigma_{y}w_{t}}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}}}. (46) The logarithm of our estimate is given by: log ⁡ b x | y LAPL , t + 1 = log ⁡ ( n x | y t + 1 ) − log ⁡ ( τ y t + M ) . \\log\\mathrm{b}_{x|y}^{\\text{\\tiny LAPL},~t+1}=\\log\\left(n_{x|y}^{t}+1\\right)-\\log\\left(\\tau_{y}^{t}+M\\right). (47) In what comes next we will denote ( ⋄ ) (\\diamond) terms that are of null average. The first terms of ( 47 ) reads: log ⁡ ( n x | y t + 1 ) ≈ log ⁡ p x | y + log ⁡ p y s ​ t + 1 p y s ​ p x | y ​ t − 1 2 ​ t ​ ( σ y 2 ​ w t + 1 2 p y s + σ x | y 2 ​ z t + 1 2 p x | y 2 ​ p y s ) + ( ⋄ ) . \\log\\left(n_{x|y}^{t}+1\\right)\\approx\\log\\mathrm{p}_{x|y}+\\log\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}t+\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}\\mathrm{p}_{x|y}t}\\\\ -\\dfrac{1}{2t}\\left(\\dfrac{\\sigma_{y}^{2}w_{t+1}^{2}}{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}}+\\dfrac{\\sigma_{x|y}^{2}z_{t+1}^{2}}{\\mathrm{p}_{x|y}^{2}\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}}\\right)+(\\diamond). (48) While the expansion of the second term of ( 47 ) yields: log ⁡ ( τ y t + M ) ≈ log ⁡ p y s ​ t + M p y s ​ t − 1 2 ​ σ y 2 ​ w t + 1 2 t ​ p y s + ( ⋄ ) . \\log\\left(\\tau_{y}^{t}+M\\right)\\approx\\log\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}t+\\dfrac{M}{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}t}-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\dfrac{\\sigma_{y}^{2}w_{t+1}^{2}}{\\sqrt{t}\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}}+(\\diamond). (49) The expansions ( 48 ) ( 49 ) are valid provided t t follows t &gt; max ⁡ [ t 1 , t 2 ] t&gt;\\mathrm{max}\\left[t_{1},t_{2}\\right] with: t 1 ≡ max x , y ​ [ 1 p y s ​ p x | y ] t 2 ≡ max x , y ​ [ 1 2 ​ 1 p y s ​ 1 − p y s p y s ​ 1 − p x | y p x | y ] . \\begin{array}[]{l}t_{1}\\equiv\\underset{x,y}{\\mathrm{max}}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{y}\\mathrm{p}_{x|y}}\\right]\\\\ t_{2}\\equiv\\underset{x,y}{