expressed as before: n x | 𝐘 t ≈ p x | 𝐘 ​ τ 𝐘 t + τ 𝐘 t ​ σ x | 𝐘 ⋅ z t τ 𝐘 t ≈ p 𝐘 s ​ t + t ​ σ 𝐘 ⋅ w t . \\begin{split}n_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}^{t}&amp;\\approx\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}\\tau_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{t}+\\sqrt{\\tau_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{t}}\\sigma_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}\\cdot z_{t}\\\\ \\tau_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{t}&amp;\\approx\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{\\mathbf{Y}}t+\\sqrt{t}\\sigma_{\\mathbf{Y}}\\cdot w_{t}\\end{split}. (53) Doing the exact same steps as above one finds that : log ⁡ p x | 𝐘 − log ⁡ b x | 𝐘 LAPL , t + 1 ≈ 1 p x | 𝐘 ​ p 𝐘 s ​ t − M p 𝐘 s ​ t − 1 2 ​ t ​ σ x | 𝐘 2 ​ z t + 1 2 p x | 𝐘 2 ​ p 𝐘 s + ( ⋄ ) , \\log\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}-\\log\\mathrm{b}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{\\tiny LAPL},~t+1}\\approx\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}~\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{s}}t}-\\dfrac{M}{\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{s}}t}\\\\ -\\dfrac{1}{2t}\\dfrac{\\sigma_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}^{2}~z_{t+1}^{2}}{\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}^{2}~\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{s}}}+(\\diamond), (54) again ( ⋄ ) (\\diamond) denotes terms that are of null average. The ensemble average is defined as : ⟨ ( ⋅ ) ⟩ ≡ ∑ x , 𝐘 p 𝐘 s ​ p x | 𝐘 ⋅ 𝔼 Z , W ​ [ ( ⋅ ) ] \\left\\langle(\\cdot)\\right\\rangle\\equiv\\sum_{x,\\mathbf{Y}}\\mathrm{p}^{\\text{s}}_{\\mathbf{Y}}~\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}\\cdot\\mathbb{E}_{Z,W}\\left[(\\cdot)\\right] . Applying this definition, remembering that: ∑ x , 𝐘 1 = M n + 1 \\sum_{x,\\mathbf{Y}}~1=M^{n+1} and ∑ x , 𝐘 p x | 𝐘 = M n \\sum_{x,\\mathbf{Y}}\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}=M^{n} , reads: ⟨ log ⁡ p x | 𝐘 − log ⁡ b x | 𝐘 LAPL , t + 1 ⟩ ≈ M n ​ ( M − 1 ) 2 ​ t . \\left\\langle\\log\\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}-\\log\\mathrm{b}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{\\tiny LAPL},~t+1}\\right\\rangle\\approx\\dfrac{M^{n}(M-1)}{2t}. (55) Summing ( 55 ) yields the expression for the regret for arbitrary correlated races: ⟨ Δ ⁡ ( t ) ⟩ = ⟨ Δ ⁡ ( t 0 ) ⟩ + M n ​ ( M − 1 ) 2 ​ log ⁡ t t 0 + 1 , \\left\\langle\\Delta(t)\\right\\rangle=\\left\\langle\\Delta(t_{0})\\right\\rangle+\\dfrac{M^{n}(M-1)}{2}\\log\\dfrac{t}{t_{0}+1}, (56) which is valid for a t 0 t_{0} following the same constraint ( 50 ) replacing p x | y \\mathrm{p}_{x|y} and p y s \\mathrm{p}_{y}^{\\text{s}} by p x | 𝐘 \\mathrm{p}_{x|\\mathbf{Y}} and p 𝐘 s \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathbf{Y}}^{\\text{s}} respectively. References References [1] Kelly J L 1956 IRE Trans. Inf. Theory 2 185–189 [2] Cover T M and Thomas J A 2005 Elements of Information Theory (Wiley Interscience) [3] Rivoire O and Leibler S 2011 J. Stat. Phys. 142 1124–1166 [4] Bergstrom C T and Lachmann M 2004 IEEE Inf. Theory Work. - Proceedings, ITW 50–54 [5] Levien E, Min J, Kondev J and Amir A 2020 Rep. Prog. Phys. 84 116601 [6] Venable D L 2007 Ecology 88 1086–1090 [7] MacLean L C, Thorp E O and Ziemba W T 2011 The Kelly capital growth investment criterion: Theory and practice vol 3 (Word Scientific) [8] Dinis L, Unterberger J and Lacoste D 2020 Europhys. Lett. 131 1–23 [9] Dinis L, Unterberger J and Lacoste D 2022 J. Stat. Mech. Theory Exp. 2022 053503 [10] Kussell E and Leibler S 2005 Science (80-. ). 309 2075–2078 [11] Perkins T J and Swain P S 2009 Mol. Syst. Biol. 5 326 [12] Cover T M 1991 Math. Financ. 1 1–29 [13] Vinkler D A, Permuter H H and Merhav N 2016 J. Stat. Mech. Theory Exp. 2016 43403 [14] Still S, Sivak D A, Bell A J and Crooks G E 2012 Phys. Rev. Lett. 109 120604 [15] Merhav N and Feder M 1998 IEEE Trans. Inf. Theory 44 2124–2147 [16] Hirono Y and Hidaka Y 2015 J. Stat. Phys. 161 721–742 [17] Jaynes E T 2003 Probability theory: The logic of science (Cambridge university press) [18] Pugatch R, Barkai N and Tlusty T 2013 Asymptotic Cellular Growth Rate as the Effective Information Utilization Rate ( Preprint ) [19] Lai T L and Robbins H 1985 Adv. Appl. Math. 6 4–22 [20] Cover T M and Ordentlich E 1996 IEEE Trans. Inf. Theory 42 348–363 [21] Permuter H H, Kim Y H and Weissman T 2011 IEEE Trans. Inf. Theory 57 3248–3259 [22] Kobayashi T Y and Sughiyama Y 2019 Entropy 21 1002 [23] Mitsokapas E and Harris R J 2022 P