valuation under incomplete information.\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)\n, 12291–12303.\nSaha and Gopalan (2020)\nSaha, A.; and Gopalan, A. 2020.\nRegret Minimization in Stochastic Contextual Dueling Bandits.\narXiv preprint arXiv:2002.08583\n.\nSaha, Koren, and Mansour (2021)\nSaha, A.; Koren, T.; and Mansour, Y. 2021.\nAdversarial dueling bandits.\nIn\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n,\n9235–9244.\nSilver et al. (2017)\nSilver, D.; Schrittwieser, J.; Simonyan, K.; Antonoglou, I.; Huang, A.; Guez,\nA.; Hubert, T.; Baker, L.; Lai, M.; and Bolton, A. 2017.\nMastering the game of Go without human knowledge.\nNature\n, 550(7676): 354.\nSzörényi et al. (2015)\nSzörényi, B.; Busa-Fekete, R.; Paul, A.; and Hüllermeier, E. 2015.\nOnline rank elicitation for plackett-luce: A dueling bandits\napproach.\nIn\nProceedings of the 19th international Conference on Neural\nInformation Processing systems (NeurIPS)\n.\nThompson (1933)\nThompson, W. R. 1933.\nOn the likelihood that one unknown probability exceeds another in\nview of the evidence of two samples.\nBiometrika\n, 25(3/4): 285–294.\nVinyals et al. (2019)\nVinyals, O.; Babuschkin, I.; Czarnecki, W. M.; Mathieu, M.; Dudzik, A.; Chung,\nJ.; Choi, D. H.; Powell, R.; Ewalds, T.; Georgiev, P.; et al. 2019.\nGrandmaster level in StarCraft II using multi-agent reinforcement\nlearning.\nNature\n, 575(7782): 350–354.\nYang et al. (2020)\nYang, Y.; Tutunov, R.; Sakulwongtana, P.; and Ammar, H. B. 2020.\nα\nα\n\\alpha^{\\alpha}\n-Rank: Practically Scaling\nα\n\\alpha\n-Rank through\nStochastic Optimisation.\nIn\nProceedings of the 19th International Conference on\nAutonomous Agents and MultiAgent Systems (AAMAS)\n, 1575–1583.\nYue et al. (2012)\nYue, Y.; Broder, J.; Kleinberg, R.; and Joachims, T. 2012.\nThe k-armed dueling bandits problem.\nJournal of Computer and System Sciences\n, 78(5): 1538–1556.\nYue and Joachims (2009)\nYue, Y.; and Joachims, T. 2009.\nInteractively optimizing information retrieval systems as a dueling\nbandits problem.\nIn\nProceedings of the 26th Annual International Conference on\nMachine Learning (ICML)\n, 1201–1208.\nAppendix A\nAdditional Details on Algorithms\nAdditional background on multi-dimensional Elo ratings (mElo)\nThe winning probability matrix\nP\nP\ncan be converted into an antisymmetric matrix\nA\n=\nσ\n−\n1\n​\n(\nP\n)\nA=\\sigma^{-1}(P)\nwith\nA\ni\n​\nj\n=\nlog\n⁡\nP\ni\n​\nj\n1\n−\nP\ni\n​\nj\nA_{ij}=\\log\\frac{P_{ij}}{1-P_{ij}}\n.\nFrom the Hodge decomposition theory\n(\nJiang et al. 2011\n)\n, the antisymmetric matrix\nA\nA\ndecomposes as\nA\n=\ng\n​\nr\n​\na\n​\nd\n​\n(\nr\n)\n+\nr\n​\no\n​\nt\n​\n(\nA\n)\nA=grad(r)+rot(A)\n, where\nr\n​\no\n​\nt\n​\n(\nA\n)\ni\n​\nj\n=\n1\nn\n​\n∑\nk\n=\n1\nn\nA\ni\n​\nj\n+\nA\nj\n​\nk\n−\nA\ni\n​\nk\nrot(A)_{ij}=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}A_{ij}+A_{jk}-A_{ik}\n, capturing the intransitive relations,\ng\n​\nr\n​\na\n​\nd\n​\n(\nr\n)\n=\nr\n⋅\n𝟏\n⊤\n−\n𝟏\n⋅\nr\n⊤\ngrad(r)=r\\cdot\\bm{1}^{\\top}-\\bm{1}\\cdot r^{\\top}\n, indicating the combination gradient of divergence vector\nr\n=\n1\nn\n​\nA\n⋅\n1\nr=\\frac{1}{n}A\\cdot 1\n.\nAccording to the Schur decomposition, mElo extends the Elo model by learning an low-rank(\n2\n​\nk\n2k\n) approximation of rotation matrix\nr\n​\no\n​\nt\n​\n(\nA\n)\nrot(A)\n, the cyclic component of\nA\nA\n.\nConsider\nA\n=\ng\n​\nr\n​\na\n​\nd\n​\n(\nr\n)\n+\nr\n​\no\n​\nt\n​\n(\nA\n)\n≈\ng\n​\nr\n​\na\n​\nd\n​\n(\nr\n)\n+\nC\nn\n×\n2\n​\nk\n​\nΩ\n2\n​\nk\n×\n2\n​\nk\n​\nC\nn\n×\n2\n​\nk\n⊤\n,\nA=grad(r)+rot(A)\\approx grad(r)+C_{n\\times 2k}\\Omega_{2k\\times 2k}C_{n\\times 2k}^{\\top},\nwhere\nΩ\n2\n​\nk\n×\n2\n​\nk\n=\n∑\ni\n=\n1\nk\n(\ne\n2\n​\ni\n−\n1\n​\ne\n2\n​\ni\n⊤\n−\ne\n2\n​\ni\n​\ne\n2\n​\ni\n−\n1\n⊤\n)\n.\n\\Omega_{2k\\times 2k}=\\sum_{i=1}^{k}(e_{2i-1}e_{2i}^{\\top}-e_{2i}e_{2i-1}^{\\top}).\nBy learning a\n2\n​\nk\n2k\n-dimensional vector\nc\nx\nc_{x}\nand a rating\nr\nx\nr_{x}\nper player, the win-loss prediction for mElo\n2k\nis defined as:\np\n^\nx\n​\ny\n=\nσ\n⁡\n(\nr\nx\n−\nr\ny\n+\nc\nx\n⊤\n⋅\nΩ\n2\n​\nk\n×\n2\n​\nk\n⋅\nc\ny\n)\n.\n\\hat{p}_{xy}=\\sigma\\left(r_{x}-r_{y}+{c}_{x}^{\\top}\\cdot{\\Omega}_{2k\\times 2k}\\cdot{c}_{y}\\right).\n(17)\nNotice that the Elo model uses\nk\n=\n0\nk=0\n.\nBased on the probability estimation function in Eq. (\n17\n), the update functions equivalent to Eq. (\n4\n) on mElo is:\nr\nx\nt\n+\n1\n\\displaystyle r_{x}^{t+1}\n=\nr\nx\nt\n+\nη\n⋅\n(\no\nx\n​\ny\nt\n−\np\n^\nx\n​\ny\nt\n)\n,\n\\displaystyle=r_{x}^{t}+\\eta\\cdot\\left(o_{xy}^{t}-\\hat{p}_{xy}^{t}\\right),\n(18)\nc\nx\nt\n+\n1\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n−\n1\n)\n\\displaystyle c_{x}^{t+1}(2i-1)\n=\nc\nx\nt\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n−\n1\n)\n+\nη\n⋅\n(\no\nx\n​\ny\nt\n−\np\n^\nx\n​\ny\nt\n)\n​\nc\ny\nt\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n)\n,\n\\displaystyle=c_{x}^{t}(2i-1)+\\eta\\cdot\\left(o^{t}_{xy}-\\hat{p}_{xy}^{t}\\right)c_{y}^{t}(2i),\n(19)\nc\nx\nt\n+\n1\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n)\n\\displaystyle c_{x}^{t+1}(2i)\n=\nc\nx\nt\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n)\n−\nη\n⋅\n(\no\nx\n​\ny\nt\n−\np\n^\nx\n​\ny\nt\n)\n​\nc\ny\nt\n​\n(\n2\n​\ni\n−\n1\n)\n.\n\\displaystyle=c_{x}^{t}(2i)-\\eta\\cdot\\left(o_{xy}^{t}-\\hat{p}_{xy}^{t}\\right)c_{y}^{t}(2i-1).\n(20)\nComparing to the Elo ratings, mElo\n2k\nadopts a different win-loss prediction function by introducing a vector\nc\nx\nc_{x}\n, but still follows the gradient descent update.\nAlgorithm for\nMaxIn-mElo\nAlgorithm\n2\ngives the details of\nMaxIn-mElo\n. Our MaxIn-mElo algorithm can be obtained by modifying the loss function, gradient and UCB score function in our MaxIn-Elo algorithm. In order to solve the intransitive games, our MaxIn-mElo employs the mElo model, and considers both the transitive and cyclic components to calculate the UCB score.\nAlgorithm 2\nMaxIn-mElo\n: Dueling bandits with online SGD for mElo.\n0:\nT\n,\nN\n,\nτ\n,\nα\n,\nγ\nT,N,\\tau,\\alpha,\\gamma\n0:\noutput\nθ\n\\theta\n1:\nRandomly choose a pair to compare and record as\nx\nt\n,\ny\nt\n,\no\nt\nx_{t},y_{t},o_{t}\nfor\nt\n∈\n[\nτ\n]\nt\\in[\\tau]\n2:\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n=\n∑\nt\n=\n1\nτ\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\n​\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\nV_{\\tau+1}=\\sum_{t=1}^{\\tau}(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})^{T}\n3:\nInitialize\n𝒓\n^\nτ\n\\hat{\\bm{r}}_{\\tau}\nby MLE as Line 3 in Alg.\n1\nand\nc\nc\n.\n4:\nMaintain convex set\n𝒞\n=\n{\nr\n:\n‖\nr\n−\nr\n^\nτ\n‖\n≤\n2\n}\n\\mathcal{C}=\\left\\{r:\\left\\|r-\\hat{r}_{\\tau}\\right\\|\\leq 2\\right\\}\n5:\nfor\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\n,\nτ\n+\n2\n,\n…\n,\nT\nt=\\tau+1,\\tau+2,\\dots,T\ndo\n6:\nif\nt\n%\n​\nτ\n=\n1\nt\\%\\tau=1\nthen\n7:\nj\n←\n⌊\n(\nt\n−\n1\n)\n/\nτ\n⌋\nj\\leftarrow\\lfloor(t-1)/\\tau\\rfloor\nand\nη\nj\n=\n1\nα\n​\nj\n\\eta_{j}=\\frac{1}{\\alpha j}\n8:\nCalculate gradient\n∇\nr\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nr\n~\nj\n−\n1\n)\n\\nabla_{r}l_{j,\\tau}(\\tilde{r}_{j-1})\naccording to Eq. (\n4\n)\n9:\nUpdate gradient\nr\n~\nj\n←\n∏\n𝒞\n(\nr\n~\nj\n−\n1\n−\nη\nj\n​\n∇\nr\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nr\n~\nj\n−\n1\n)\n)\n\\tilde{r}_{j}\\leftarrow\\prod_{\\mathcal{C}}\\left(\\tilde{r}_{j-1}-\\eta_{j}\\nabla_{r}l_{j,\\tau}(\\tilde{r}_{j-1})\\right)\n10:\nCompute\nr\n¯\n=\n1\nj\n​\n∑\nq\n=\n1\nj\nr\n~\nq\n\\bar{r}=\\frac{1}{j}\\sum_{q=1}^{j}\\tilde{r}_{q}\n11:\nCalculate gradient\n∇\nC\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nC\n~\nj\n−\n1\n)\n\\nabla_{C}l_{j,\\tau}(\\tilde{C}_{j-1})\n12:\nUpdate gradient\nC\n~\nj\n←\nC\n~\nj\n−\n1\n−\nη\nj\n​\n∇\nC\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nC\n~\nj\n−\n1\n)\n\\tilde{C}_{j}\\leftarrow\\tilde{C}_{j-1}-\\eta_{j}\\nabla_{C}l_{j,\\tau}(\\tilde{C}_{j-1})\n13:\nend\nif\n14:\nDefine a candidate optimal set\n𝒮\n=\n{\nx\n|\nr\n¯\nx\n−\nr\n¯\ny\n+\nc\n¯\nx\nT\n𝛀\nc\n¯\ny\n+\nγ\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n>\n0\n,\n∀\ny\n∈\n[\nn\n]\n/\n{\nx\n}\n}\n\\mathcal{S}=\\{x\\ |\\ \\bar{r}_{x}-\\bar{r}_{y}+\\bar{c}_{x}^{T}\\bm{\\Omega}\\bar{c}_{y}+\\gamma\\ \\left\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}>0,\\ \\forall y\\in[n]/\\{x\\}\\}\n15:\nSelect a pair\n(\nx\nt\n,\ny\nt\n)\n=\narg\n⁡\nmax\n(\nx\n,\ny\n)\n∈\n𝒮\n⁡\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n(x_{t},y_{t})=\\argmax_{(x,y)\\in\\mathcal{S}}\\left\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\n.\n16:\nPull arms\n(\nx\nt\n,\ny\nt\n)\n(x_{t},y_{t})\nand observe\no\nt\n​\n(\nx\nt\n,\ny\nt\n)\no_{t}(x_{t},y_{t})\n17:\nCompute\nV\nt\n+\n1\n=\nV\nt\n+\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\n​\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\nV_{t+1}=V_{t}+(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})^{T}\n18:\nend\nfor\nTable 2:\nStatistics of twelve real world games.\n|\nTop SSCC\n|\n|\\text{Top SSCC}|\nindicates the size of the SSCC with best performance.\nGame\n# Policies\n|\nTop SSCC\n|\n|\\text{Top SSCC}|\nTransitivity\nTransitive game\n100\n1\nYes\nTriangular game\n100\n1\nYes\nElo game\n100\n1\nYes\nElo game + noise=0.01\n100\n1\nYes\nElo game + noise=0.05\n100\n1\nYes\nElo game + noise=0.1\n100\n1\nYes\nKuhn-poker\n64\n64\nNo\nAlphaStar\n100\n1\nNo\ntic\n_\n\\_\ntac_toe\n100\n2\nNo\nhex(board_size=3)\n100\n2\nNo\nBlotto\n100\n99\nNo\n5,3-Blotto\n21\n18\nNo\nFigure 5:\nAdditional results of different\nγ\n\\gamma\nof our\nMaxIn-Elo\nunder top-\nk\nk\nperformance. The best top-1 curves are in dashed lines. The best top-\nk\nk\ncurves are in bold.\nFigure 6:\nResults of different parameters of\nC\nC\nof\nMaxIn-mElo\n.\nFigure 7:\nResults of different batch size\nτ\n\\tau\nof\nMaxIn-Elo\non Elo game and\nMaxIn-mElo\non Kuhn-poker.\nAppendix B\nAdditional Experiments\nTable\n2\ngives the details of the games used in experiments. The sizes of the top SSCC of six transitive games are equal to 1, which indicates that there exists a top player and its winning probabilities against other players are greater than\n0.5\n0.5\n. For the intransitive games, the top SSCC size of AlphaStar is equal to 1, but there also exist cycles among players outside of the top SSCC. The top SSCC is the smallest set of players such that the winning probabilities of outside players against inside players are less than 0.5.\nFigure\n5\nshows the comparison between different\nγ\n\\gamma\nof\nMaxIn-Elo\nunder top-\nk\nk\nidentification.\nγ\n\\gamma\ntrade off exploration and exploitation in selecting arm-pairs. Smaller\nγ\n\\gamma\nleads to tighter candidate sets then leads to better top-1 performance, but too small\nγ\n\\gamma\nmay result in that the top player is excluded from the candidate set.\nOn Elo game, its three variants and Triangular game,\nMaxIn-Elo\nhas the best performance when\nγ\n=\n0.6\n\\gamma=0.6\n. The performance of top-1 gradually drops with\nγ\n\\gamma\nincreasing. But it misidentifies the best player when\nγ\n=\n0.4\n\\gamma=0.4\n.\nBy contrast, larger\nγ\n\\gamma\nleads to larger candidate set then lead to better top-\nk\nk\nperformance, but too large\nγ\n\\gamma\nresults in much useless exploration on top players identification. In general, larger\nγ\n\\gamma\nhas better top-\nk\nk\nperformance, but\nγ\n=\n1.2\n\\gamma=1.2\nis worse than\nγ\n=\n1\n\\gamma=1\nbecause of too large candidate set and too much exploration. On Elo game,\nMaxIn-Elo\nhas best top-\n1\n1\nperformance on\nγ\n=\n0.6\n\\gamma=0.6\n, best top-\nk\nk\nperformance on\nγ\n=\n1\n\\gamma=1\n, and\nγ\n=\n0.8\n\\gamma=0.8\nbalances the top-1 and top-\nk\nk\nidentification. On Transitive game,\nMaxIn-Elo\nhas best top-\n1\n1\nand top-\nk\nk\nperformance when\nγ\n=\n0.4\n\\gamma=0.4\n.\nFigure\n6\ngives results\nMaxIn-mElo\nwith different dimensions of\nc\nc\n.\nOverall,\nC\n=\n8\nC=8\nreturns best performance. The performance of top-1 identification and cumulative of\nMaxIn-mElo\ngradually increases as the dimension\nC\nC\nincreases, but the performance drops when\nC\n=\n16\nC=16\n.\nIn general, larger\nC\nC\nleads to better approximation of the intransitive skills, but this also requires more samples for training.\nFigure\n7\nshows results of\nMaxIn-Elo\non Elo game and of\nMaxIn-mElo\non Kuhn-poker with different batch size\nτ\n\\tau\n. When the batch size\nτ\n=\n1\n\\tau=1\n, both\nMaxIn-Elo\nand\nMaxIn-mElo\nhave bad performance on top-1 player identification and large cumulative reward, which may because of that the objective function is not strongly convex and hard to convergence under this setting. On the other hand, when selecting too large\nτ\n\\tau\n, such as\n4.0\n​\nn\n,\n8.0\n​\nn\n4.0n,\\ 8.0n\n, the number of updates is less than that of small\nτ\n\\tau\nwith the same sampling rounds. The\nMaxIn-Elo\non the transitive Elo game gets satisfactory top-1 identification and regret performance at around\nτ\n=\n0.5\n​\nn\n​\n1.0\n​\nn\n\\tau=0.5n~1.0n\n, and the\nMaxIn-Elo\non the intransitive Kuhn-poker obtains best top identification and regret performance at around\nτ\n=\n0.7\n​\nn\n\\tau=0.7n\n.\nAppendix C\nTheories and Proofs\nWe provide detailed proofs below.\nProofs of Lemmas\nProposition 1\n(\n(\nSaha and Gopalan 2020\n)\n)\n.\nWe select a batch of feature vectors\nX\n1\n,\nX\n2\n,\n…\n,\nX\nτ\n{X_{1},X_{2},\\dots,X_{\\tau}}\nfrom a distribution\nv\nv\nand\n‖\nX\n‖\n≤\n2\n\\|X\\|\\leq 2\n. Let\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n=\n∑\nt\n=\n1\nτ\n(\nX\nt\n​\nX\nt\n⊤\n)\nV_{\\tau+1}=\\sum_{t=1}^{\\tau}(X_{t}X_{t}^{\\top})\n,\nΣ\n=\n𝔼\nX\n​\n∼\ni\n​\ni\n​\nd\n​\nv\n​\n[\nX\n​\nX\n⊤\n]\n\\Sigma=\\mathbb{E}_{X\\overset{iid}{\\sim}v}[XX^{\\top}]\n. There exist two positive constant\nC\n1\n,\nC\n2\nC_{1},C_{2}\nsuch that if the batch size\nτ\n\\tau\nis appropriately selected as\nτ\n≥\n2\n​\n(\nC\n1\n​\nn\n+\nC\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\n1\n/\nδ\n)\nλ\nmin\n​\n(\nΣ\n)\n)\n2\n+\n4\n​\nC\nλ\nmin\n​\n(\nΣ\n)\n\\tau\\geq 2\\left(\\frac{C_{1}\\sqrt{n}+C_{2}\\sqrt{\\log(1/\\delta)}}{\\lambda_{\\min}(\\Sigma)}\\right)^{2}+\\frac{4C}{\\lambda_{\\min}(\\Sigma)}\n, then\nλ\nmin\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n≥\nC\n\\lambda_{\\min}(V_{\\tau+1})\\geq C\nholds with probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nδ\n1-\\frac{1}{\\delta}\n.\nThe Proposition\n1\nprovides guidance about the selection of batch size\nτ\n\\tau\nand is a corollary of Lemma 12 in\n(\nSaha and Gopalan 2020\n)\n.\nIn Algorithm\n1\n, the first batch of pairs are randomly selected for initializing the maximum likelihood estimator, the rest batches of pairs are selected with maximum uncertainty based on UCB estimation.\nThe batch size\nτ\n\\tau\ncan be suitably to achieve low MLE error and the\nα\n\\alpha\n-strongly convex condition.\nSee\n1\nProof of Lemma\n1\n.\nOur setting is a special case of generalized linear bandits(GLM)\n(\nLi, Lu, and Zhou 2017\n)\n, and we can directly get our Lemma\n1\nby substitute\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\ne_{x}-e_{y}\ninto Lemma 2 of\n(\nLi, Lu, and Zhou 2017\n)\n.\nAccording to\n(\nLi, Lu, and Zhou 2017\n)\n, we have\n∑\ni\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nτ\n+\nt\n‖\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n‖\nV\ni\n−\n1\n2\n≤\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\ndet\n⁡\nV\nt\n+\n1\ndet\n⁡\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n≤\n2\n​\nd\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\ntr\n⁡\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n+\nt\nd\n)\n−\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\ndet\n⁡\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n.\n\\sum_{i=\\tau+1}^{\\tau+t}\\left\\|e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}}\\right\\|_{V_{i}^{-1}}^{2}\\leq 2\\log\\frac{\\operatorname{det}V_{t+1}}{\\operatorname{det}V_{\\tau+1}}\\leq 2d\\log\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{tr}\\left(V_{\\tau+1}\\right)+t}{d}\\right)-2\\log\\operatorname{det}V_{\\tau+1}.\n(21)\nThe trace of\nV\nτ\n+\n1\nV_{\\tau+1}\nis\ntr\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n=\n∑\ni\n=\n1\nτ\ntr\n​\n(\n(\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n)\n​\n(\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n)\n⊤\n)\n=\n∑\ni\n=\n1\nτ\n‖\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n‖\n2\n=\n2\n​\nτ\n\\text{tr}(V_{\\tau+1})=\\sum_{i=1}^{\\tau}\\text{tr}\\left((e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}})(e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}})^{\\top}\\right)=\\sum_{i=1}^{\\tau}\\left\\|e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}}\\right\\|^{2}=2\\tau\n, and the determinant satisfies\nd\n​\ne\n​\nt\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n=\n∏\ni\n=\n1\nd\nλ\ni\n≥\nλ\nmin\nd\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n≥\n1\ndet(V_{\\tau+1})=\\prod_{i=1}^{d}\\lambda_{i}\\geq\\lambda_{\\min}^{d}\\left(V_{\\tau+1}\\right)\\geq 1\nfor we assume\nλ\nmin\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n≥\n1\n\\lambda_{\\min}(V_{\\tau+1})\\geq 1\n, where\n{\nλ\ni\n}\n\\{\\lambda_{i}\\}\nare the eigenvalues of\nV\nτ\n+\n1\nV_{\\tau+1}\n.\nApplying the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n∑\ni\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nτ\n+\nt\n‖\n(\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n)\n‖\nV\ni\n−\n1\n≤\nt\n​\n∑\ni\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nt\n‖\n(\ne\nx\ni\n−\ne\ny\ni\n)\n‖\nV\ni\n−\n1\n2\n≤\n2\n​\nt\n​\nd\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nt\n+\n2\n​\nτ\nd\n)\n\\sum_{i=\\tau+1}^{\\tau+t}\\left\\|(e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}})\\right\\|_{V_{i}^{-1}}\\leq\\sqrt{t\\sum_{i=\\tau+1}^{t}\\left\\|(e_{x_{i}}-e_{y_{i}})\\right\\|_{V_{i}^{-1}}^{2}}\\leq\\sqrt{2td\\log\\left(\\frac{t+2\\tau}{d}\\right)}\n(22)\nThus the proof of Lemma\n1\nis complete.\n∎\nSee\n2\nProof of Lemma\n2\n.\nRelying on the Lemma 1 in\n(\nDing, Hsieh, and Sharpnack 2021\n)\nand Proposition\n1\n, we set the batch size\nτ\n≥\nτ\n1\n\\tau\\geq\\tau_{1}\nin Eq. (\n14\n), thus we have\n‖\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\n≤\n1\n\\|\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*}\\|\\leq 1\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\nfor any\nj\n≥\n1\nj\\geq 1\n. So we have\n‖\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n^\nτ\n‖\n≤\n2\n\\|\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-\\hat{r}_{\\tau}\\|\\leq 2\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n2\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{2}{T^{2}}\n. In Algorithm\n1\n, we project the SGD estimation\nr\n~\nj\n\\tilde{r}_{j}\ninto the convex hall\n𝒞\n=\n{\nr\n:\n‖\nr\n−\nr\n^\nτ\n‖\n≤\n2\n}\n\\mathcal{C}=\\{r:\\|r-\\hat{r}_{\\tau}\\|\\leq 2\\}\n, thus we have\nr\n~\nj\n∈\n{\nr\n:\n‖\nr\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\n≤\n3\n}\n\\tilde{r}_{j}\\in\\{r:\\|r-{r}^{*}\\|\\leq 3\\}\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\n. And from Proposition 1, if the batch size\nτ\n≥\nτ\n2\n\\tau\\geq\\tau_{2}\ndefined in Eq. (\n14\n), then\nλ\nmin\n​\n(\n∑\nt\n=\n(\nj\n−\n1\n)\n​\nτ\n+\n1\nj\n​\nτ\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\n​\n(\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\n⊤\n)\n≥\nα\nc\n3\n\\lambda_{\\min}(\\sum_{t=(j-1)\\tau+1}^{j\\tau}(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})(e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}})^{\\top})\\geq\\frac{\\alpha}{c_{3}}\nholds with probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\n. Thus with probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\n, the objective function\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nr\n)\nl_{j,\\tau}(r)\nin Eq. (\n7\n) is an\nα\n\\alpha\n-strongly convex function when\nr\n∈\n{\nr\n:\n‖\nr\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\n≤\n3\n}\nr\\in\\{r:\\|r-r^{*}\\|\\leq 3\\}\n.\nRelying on the above analysis and according to Lemma 2 in\n(\nDing, Hsieh, and Sharpnack 2021\n)\n, we have that if the batch size\nτ\n\\tau\nis chosen as Eq. (\n14\n), then the convergence rate of the\nα\n\\alpha\n-strongly convex objective function\nl\nj\n,\nτ\n​\n(\nr\n)\nl_{j,\\tau}(r)\nsatisfies that\n‖\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n‖\n≤\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\nj\n\\left\\|\\bar{r}_{j}-\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}\\right\\|\\leq\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\log j}{j}}\n(23)\nfor all\nj\n≥\n1\nj\\geq 1\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n3\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{3}{T^{2}}\n.\nFrom Proposition\n1\nand\nτ\n≥\nτ\n1\n\\tau\\geq\\tau_{1}\nin Eq. (\n14\n), we have\nλ\nm\n​\ni\n​\nn\n​\n(\nV\nτ\n+\n1\n)\n≥\n4\n​\n(\nn\n+\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\nT\n)\nc\n1\n2\n≥\n1\n\\lambda_{min}(V_{\\tau+1})\\geq\\frac{4(n+2\\log T)}{c_{1}^{2}}\\geq 1\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\nbecause\nc\n1\nc_{1}\nis upper bounded by\n1\n4\n\\frac{1}{4}\n. Then according to the Lemma 3 in\n(\nLi, Lu, and Zhou 2017\n)\n, we have that the event\nℰ\n=\n{\n‖\nr\n^\nt\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\nV\nt\n≤\n1\n2\n​\nc\n1\n​\nn\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\n1\n+\n2\n​\nt\nn\n)\n+\n2\n​\nlog\n⁡\nT\n,\nt\n≥\nτ\n}\n\\mathcal{E}=\\{\\|\\hat{r}_{t}-r^{*}\\|_{V_{t}}\\leq\\frac{1}{2c_{1}}\\sqrt{\\frac{n}{2}\\log\\left(1+\\frac{2t}{n}\\right)+2\\log T},t\\geq\\tau\\}\n(24)\nholds with probability at least\n1\n−\n2\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{2}{T^{2}}\n.\nCombining the Eq. (\n23\n) and Eq. (\n24\n) and applying the union bound, we can get that for all\nt\n≥\nτ\nt\\geq\\tau\nthe event\nE\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\nE_{1}(t)\nholds with probability at least\n1\n−\n5\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{5}{T^{2}}\n.\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n≤\n\\displaystyle|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\bar{r}_{j}-r^{*})|\\leq\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n|\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n\\displaystyle|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\bar{r}_{j}-\\hat{r}_{j\\tau})|+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*})|\n(25)\n≤\n(\n1\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(1)}}{{\\leq}}\n2\n​\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\nj\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n\\displaystyle\\sqrt{2}\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\log j}{j}}+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*})|\n=\n\\displaystyle=\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*})|\n≤\n(\n2\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(2)}}{{\\leq}}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\n‖\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+\\|\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}}\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}\n≤\n(\n3\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(3)}}{{\\leq}}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}\nInequality (1) holds because the Eq. (\n23\n); inequality (2) is due to the Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, where\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\nV_{j\\tau+1}\nis a positive definite matrix with probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\n. (3) holds from the Eq. (\n24\n).\n∎\nSee\n3\nProof of Lemma\n3\n.\nFollowing the proof of Lemma\n2\n, for any\nj\n≥\n1\nj\\geq 1\nwe have that:\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n≤\n\\displaystyle|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\bar{r}_{j}-r^{*})|\\leq\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n|\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n∗\n−\nr\n^\nt\n−\n1\n)\n|\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nt\n−\n1\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n\\displaystyle|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\bar{r}_{j}-\\hat{r}_{j\\tau})|+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*})|+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(r^{*}-\\hat{r}_{t-1})|+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{t-1}-r^{*})|\n(26)\n≤\n\\displaystyle{\\leq}\n2\n​\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\nj\n+\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n+\n2\n​\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n^\nt\n−\n1\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n\\displaystyle\\sqrt{2}\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\log j}{j}}+|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-{r}^{*})|+2|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}(\\hat{r}_{t-1}-r^{*})|\n≤\n(\n1\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(1)}}{{\\leq}}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\n‖\nr\n^\nj\n​\nτ\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\n‖\nr\n^\nt\n−\nr\n∗\n‖\nV\nt\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+\\|\\hat{r}_{j\\tau}-r^{*}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}}\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+\\|\\hat{r}_{t}-r^{*}\\|_{V_{t}}\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\n≤\n(\n2\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(2)}}{{\\leq}}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\n≤\n(\n3\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(3)}}{{\\leq}}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n2\n​\nn\n​\nj\n​\nτ\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\n(\nj\n+\n1\n)\n​\nτ\n+\n1\nn\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\sqrt{2nj\\tau\\log\\left(\\frac{(j+1)\\tau+1}{n}\\right)}+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\n≤\n\\displaystyle{\\leq}\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\n2\n​\nn\n​\nT\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nT\n+\nτ\nn\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(T)\\sqrt{2nT\\log\\left(\\frac{T+\\tau}{n}\\right)}+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\nInequality (1) is due to the Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, where\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\nV_{j\\tau+1}\nand\nV\nt\nV_{t}\nis a positive definite matrix with probability at least\n1\n−\n1\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{1}{T^{2}}\n. (2) holds because the Eq. (\n24\n). (3) holds from the Lemma\n1\n.\nDefine the constant\nC\n=\n2\n​\nn\n​\nT\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nT\n+\nτ\nn\n)\nC=\\sqrt{2nT\\log\\left(\\frac{T+\\tau}{n}\\right)}\n, the inequality\n|\n(\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n|\n≤\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\n2\n​\nn\n​\nT\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nT\n+\nτ\nn\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\left|(e_{x}-e_{y})^{T}\\left(\\bar{r}_{j}-r^{*}\\right)\\right|\\leq g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(T)\\sqrt{2nT\\log\\left(\\frac{T+\\tau}{n}\\right)}+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\nholds with high probability as above derivation.\nThis is equivalent to the following:\n(\ne\ny\n−\ne\nx\n∗\n)\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n≤\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\nC\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n\\displaystyle(e_{y}-e_{x^{*}})(\\bar{r}_{j}-r^{*})\\leq g_{2}(j)\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{j}}+g_{1}(T)C+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\n(27)\n⇒\n\\displaystyle\\Rightarrow\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\n)\n​\n(\nr\n¯\nj\n−\nr\n∗\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\nC\n≥\n0\n\\displaystyle(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y})(\\bar{r}_{j}-r^{*})+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}+g_{1}(T)C\\geq 0\n⇒\n\\displaystyle\\Rightarrow\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\ny\n)\n−\nr\n∗\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n+\nr\n∗\n​\n(\ny\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\nC\n≥\n0\n\\displaystyle\\bar{r}_{j}(x^{*})-\\bar{r}_{j}(y)-r^{*}(x^{*})+r^{*}(y)+2g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}+g_{1}(T)C\\geq 0\n⇒\n\\displaystyle\\Rightarrow\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\ny\n)\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n≥\nr\n∗\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n∗\n​\n(\ny\n)\n−\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n−\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\nC\n\\displaystyle\\bar{r}_{j}(x^{*})-\\bar{r}_{j}(y)+g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\\geq r^{*}(x^{*})-r^{*}(y)-g_{2}(j)\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}-g_{1}(T)C\n⇒\n\\displaystyle\\Rightarrow\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n​\n(\ny\n)\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n≥\nr\n∗\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n∗\n​\n(\ny\n)\n−\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\n​\n2\nj\n−\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\nC\n\\displaystyle\\bar{r}_{j}(x^{*})-\\bar{r}_{j}(y)+g_{1}(t)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}\\geq r^{*}(x^{*})-r^{*}(y)-\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{1+\\log j}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}-g_{1}(T)C\n⇒\n(\n1\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(1)}}{{\\Rightarrow}}\nh\n⁡\n(\nx\n∗\n,\ny\n)\n≥\nr\n∗\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n∗\n​\n(\ny\n)\n−\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\n​\n2\nj\n−\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\nC\n\\displaystyle h(x^{*},y)\\geq r^{*}(x^{*})-r^{*}(y)-\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{1+\\log j}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}-g_{1}(j)C\n⇒\n(\n2\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(2)}}{{\\Rightarrow}}\nh\n⁡\n(\nx\n∗\n,\ny\n)\n≥\nΔ\n−\nτ\nα\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\n​\n2\nj\n−\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\nC\n≥\n(\n3\n)\n0\n\\displaystyle h(x^{*},y)\\geq\\Delta-\\frac{\\tau}{\\alpha}\\sqrt{1+\\log j}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{j}}-g_{1}(j)C\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(3)}}{{\\geq}}0\n⇒\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle}}{{\\Rightarrow}}\nh\n⁡\n(\nx\n∗\n,\ny\n)\n≥\n0\n.\n\\displaystyle h(x^{*},y)\\geq 0.\nInequality (1) holds for\nγ\n=\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n)\n\\gamma=2g_{1}(t)\nand the definition of\nh\n⁡\n(\nx\n,\ny\n)\nh(x,y)\nin Eq. (\n9\n); (2) follows from\nΔ\n\\Delta\nis the difference between optimal and sub-optimal arms, so\n∀\ny\n∈\n[\nn\n]\n/\nx\n∗\n,\nΔ\n≤\nr\n∗\n​\n(\nx\n∗\n)\n−\nr\n∗\n​\n(\ny\n)\n\\forall y\\in[n]/{x^{*}},\\ \\Delta\\leq r^{*}(x^{*})-r^{*}(y)\n. (3) holds when\nα\n≥\n2\n​\nτ\n​\n1\n+\nlog\n⁡\nj\n(\nΔ\n−\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\nC\n)\n​\nj\n\\alpha\\geq\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\tau\\sqrt{1+\\log j}}{(\\Delta-g_{1}(j)C)\\sqrt{j}}\nand\nΔ\n>\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\nC\n\\Delta>g_{1}(j)C\n.\n∎\nProofs of Theorem\n1\nProof of theorem\n1\n.\nWe use\nb\nt\nb_{t}\nto denote the regret at round\nt\nt\nand recall that\nb\nt\n=\nr\nx\n∗\n∗\n−\n1\n2\n​\n(\nr\nx\nt\n∗\n+\nr\ny\nt\n∗\n)\n=\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n∗\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n∗\n2\n,\nb_{t}=r^{*}_{x^{*}}-\\frac{1}{2}(r^{*}_{x_{t}}+r^{*}_{y_{t}})=\\frac{(e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}})^{T}r^{*}+(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}})^{T}r^{*}}{2},\nand the index of batch is\nj\n=\n⌊\n(\nt\n−\n1\n)\n/\nτ\n⌋\nj=\\lfloor(t-1)/\\tau\\rfloor\n.\nThen we have that when\nt\n>\nτ\nt>\\tau\n:\n2\n​\nb\nt\n\\displaystyle 2b_{t}\n=\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n∗\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n∗\n\\displaystyle=\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right)^{T}{r}^{*}+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right)^{T}r^{*}\n(28)\n=\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n¯\nj\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n∗\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n)\n\\displaystyle=\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\bar{r}_{j}+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\left(r^{*}-\\bar{r}_{j}\\right)\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\n​\nr\n¯\nj\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n∗\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n)\n\\displaystyle+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\bar{r}_{j}+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\left(r^{*}-\\bar{r}_{j}\\right)\n≤\n(\n1\n)\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n∗\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n)\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(1)}}{{\\leq}}\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\left(r^{*}-\\bar{r}_{j}\\right)\n+\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\n(\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n)\nT\n​\n(\nr\n∗\n−\nr\n¯\nj\n)\n\\displaystyle+\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+\\left(e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right)^{T}\\left(r^{*}-\\bar{r}_{j}\\right)\n≤\n(\n2\n)\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\nx\nt\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(2)}}{{\\leq}}\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{x_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\n+\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\n∗\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n\\displaystyle+\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x^{*}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\n≤\n(\n3\n)\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(3)}}{{\\leq}}\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\n+\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n​\n(\nj\n​\nτ\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n2\nj\n\\displaystyle+\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\nInequality (1) holds for\nx\nt\n,\ny\nt\nx_{t},y_{t}\nbelong to candidate set\n𝒮\n\\mathcal{S}\n, inequality (2) holds with probability at least\n1\n−\n5\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{5}{T^{2}}\nfollowing from Lemma\n2\n.\nInequality (3) holds according to Lemma\n3\nwhere\nwe have\nx\n∗\n∈\n𝒮\nx^{*}\\in\\mathcal{S}\nwith probability at least\n1\n−\n5\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{5}{T^{2}}\nand our arm-pair selection strategy.\nBy above analysis, we have Eq. (\n28\n) holds with probability at least\n1\n−\n10\nT\n2\n1-\\frac{10}{T^{2}}\nat each round\nt\nt\n.\nNext, we give the results on cumulative regret bound:\nR\n⁡\n(\nT\n)\n\\displaystyle R(T)\n=\n∑\nt\n=\n1\nτ\nb\nt\n+\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\nb\nt\n\\displaystyle=\\sum_{t=1}^{\\tau}b_{t}+\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}b_{t}\n(29)\n≤\n(\n1\n)\nτ\n∗\nΔ\nmax\n+\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\nb\nt\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(1)}}{{\\leq}}\\tau*\\Delta_{\\max}+\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}b_{t}\n≤\n(\n2\n)\nτ\n∗\nΔ\nmax\n+\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\n1\n2\n[\nγ\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n(\nj\nτ\n)\n∥\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n∥\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n(\nj\n)\n2\nj\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(2)}}{{\\leq}}\\tau*\\Delta_{\\max}+\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}\\frac{1}{2}\\big[\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\n+\nγ\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\ng\n1\n(\nj\nτ\n)\n∥\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n∥\nV\nj\n​\nτ\n+\n1\n−\n1\n+\ng\n2\n(\nj\n)\n2\nj\n]\n\\displaystyle+\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+g_{1}(j\\tau)\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{j\\tau+1}^{-1}}+g_{2}(j)\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{j}}\\big]\n≤\n(\n3\n)\nτ\n∗\nΔ\nmax\n+\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\nγ\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\nτ\n​\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\ng\n1\n​\n(\nt\n−\n1\n)\n​\n‖\ne\nx\nt\n−\ne\ny\nt\n‖\nV\nt\n−\n1\n+\n2\n​\ng\n2\n​\n(\nj\n)\n​\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\n1\nj\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(3)}}{{\\leq}}\\tau*\\Delta_{\\max}+\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}\\gamma\\left\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\right\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+\\tau\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}g_{1}(t-1)\\|e_{x_{t}}-e_{y_{t}}\\|_{V_{t}^{-1}}+2g_{2}(j)\\sum_{t=\\tau+1}^{T}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{j}}\n≤\n(\n4\n)\nτ\n∗\nΔ\nmax\n+\n2\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\n2\n​\nn\n​\nT\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nτ\n+\nT\nn\n)\n+\nτ\n​\ng\n1\n​\n(\nT\n)\n​\n2\n​\nn\n​\nT\n​\nlog\n⁡\n(\nτ\n+\nT\nn\n)\n+\n2\n​\ng\n2\n​\n(\nJ\n)\n​\n∑\nt\n=\nτ\n+\n1\nT\n1\nj\n\\displaystyle\\stackrel{{\\scriptstyle(4)}}{