based on an implicit relation, and Company 4 is a neighbor of Company 1 based on meta-relation CEC . Each intra-class relation represents one semantic interaction, and we apply relation-specific attention to encode this characteristic. We first calculate the attention value of entity u ~ \\tilde{u} with relation ϕ k \\phi_{k} to entity u u as follows: (14) α u ​ u ~ ϕ k = exp ( LeakyRelu ( 𝐚 ϕ k ⊤ ⋅ [ 𝐖𝐳 u ∥ 𝐖𝐳 u ~ ] ) ) ∑ u ′ ∈ 𝒩 intra ϕ k ​ ( u ) exp ( LeakyRelu ( 𝐚 ϕ k ⊤ ⋅ [ 𝐖𝐳 u ∥ 𝐖𝐳 u ′ ] ) ) , \\alpha_{u\\tilde{u}}^{\\phi_{k}}=\\frac{\\exp{(\\text{LeakyRelu}({\\bf a}_{\\phi_{k}}^{\\top}\\cdot[{\\bf W}{\\bf z}_{u}\\|{\\bf W}{\\bf z}_{\\tilde{u}}]))}}{\\sum\\limits_{u^{\\prime}\\in{\\mathcal{N}}_{\\text{intra}}^{\\phi_{k}}(u)}\\exp{(\\text{LeakyRelu}({\\bf a}_{\\phi_{k}}^{\\top}\\cdot[{\\bf W}{\\bf z}_{u}\\|{\\bf W}{\\bf z}_{u^{\\prime}}]))}}\\ , where 𝐳 u {\\bf z}_{u} and 𝐳 u ~ {\\bf z}_{\\tilde{u}} are output representations of the inter-class attention, respectively. 𝐖 ∈ ℝ F ′ × F ′ {\\bf W}\\in{\\mathbb{R}}^{F^{\\prime}\\times F^{\\prime}} is a trainable weight matrix which is shared to every node of the same type. 𝐚 ϕ k ∈ ℝ 2 ​ F ′ {\\bf a}_{\\phi_{k}}\\in{\\mathbb{R}}^{2F^{\\prime}} is the node-level attention weight vector for relation ϕ k \\phi_{k} . 𝒩 intra ϕ k ​ ( u ) {\\mathcal{N}}_{\\text{intra}}^{\\phi_{k}}(u) denotes the intra-class neighbors of u u under relation ϕ k \\phi_{k} . The embedding 𝐡 u ϕ k {\\bf h}_{u}^{\\phi_{k}} of entity u u for the given relation ϕ k \\phi_{k} is calculated as follows. (15) 𝐡 u ϕ k = σ ⁡ ( ∑ u ~ ∈ 𝒩 intra ϕ k ​ ( u ) α u ​ u ~ ϕ k ⋅ 𝐖𝐳 u ~ ) , {\\bf h}_{u}^{\\phi_{k}}=\\sigma\\Big(\\sum_{\\tilde{u}\\in{\\mathcal{N}}_{\\text{intra}}^{\\phi_{k}}(u)}\\alpha_{u\\tilde{u}}^{\\phi_{k}}\\cdot{\\bf W}{\\bf z}_{\\tilde{u}}\\Big)\\ , where σ \\sigma is a non-linear activation. In total, we can get | Φ intra τ ⁡ ( u ) | |\\Phi_{\\text{intra}}^{\\tau(u)}| embeddings for entity u u . Then, we conduct relation-level attentions to