lement on various devices.\n\n\nTable 11 Comparison between Jetson Modules and GPU-Constrained Devices\n                 Jetson TX1           Jetson TX2          Jetson     AGX     Raspberry     Pi   Latte Panda       Odroid Xu4\n                                                          Xavier             Series\n CPU             Quad core ARM        Dual         core   64 bit CPU and     63-bit quad core   Intel    Cherry   Cortex A7 octa\n                 Processor.           Denver CPU and      8-core ARM         ARM                Train quad core   core CPU\n                                      quad core ARM                                             CPU\n                                      57\n GPU             NVidia Maxwell       NVidia   Pascall    Tensor cores +     -                  -                 -\n                 with         CUDA    with     CUDA       512-core   Volta\n                 cores                cores               GPU\n Memory          4GB Memory           8 GB Memory         16 GB Memory       1 GB Memory        4 GB Memory       Stacked memory\n                                                                                                                  of 2 Giga bytes.\n Storage         16      GB   Flash   32 GB storage       32 GB storage      Support Micro SD   64 GB storage     Support    Micro\n                 Storage                                                     card                                 SD Card\n Possible Deep   YOLO v2 and v3, tiny YOLO v3, SSD, Faster –RCNN and         YOLO, YOLO v2 and SSD-MobileNet etc.\n Learning        Tracking algorithm like YOLOv3+Deep SORT, YOLOv4,\n Algorithms to   YOLOR.\n Implement.\n\fField Programmable Gate Array (FPGA) has also been used in sports involving 3D motion capturing, object\nmovement analysis and image recognition, etc. Table 12 describes how different researchers performed\nvarious problem statements of sports on hardware platforms such as FPGA, GPU-based devices and their\nresults in terms of performance measures are listed.\n\nTable 12 Performance of various studies on hardware platforms\n\n                       GPU Based Work    Embedded                                              Performance\n         Ref               Station       platform          Problem Statement                     measures             Result\n  L Wu et al. 2019      NVidia Titan X              Events classifications in basketball\n        [27]                GPU.            -                        videos.                Average Accuracy         58.10%\n                                                      Basketball trajectory prediction\n  Yu Z et al. 2018                                   based on real data and generating     Measured in terms of\n        [36]           NVIDIA GTX 960       -             new trajectory samples.                  AUC               91.00%\n                                                                                           The result shows the\n                                                                                                three-level\n                                                                                           identification system      4.14%,\n                                                    Recognizing swimming styles of a       in Average, Minimum        2.16%,\n T Liang 2020 [279]\n                              -           FPGA                   swimmer.                  and Maximum offset.        5.77%.\n     J Hou et al.                                                                                                    85% and\n     2020[194]                              -                                              Recall and Specificity     96.6%\n                                                      Tracking ball movements and\n Y Yoon et al. 2019    NVidia GeForce       -           classification of players in                                74.3% and\n     