ing. In Integrating Renewables in Electricity Markets (pp. 15–56). Springer. NUMERAI [2022] NUMERAI (2022). NUMERAI, the hardest data science tournament on the planet. https://numer.ai/ . Accessed: 2022-01-07. Ospina &amp; Ferrari [2010] Ospina, R., &amp; Ferrari, S. L. (2010). Inflated beta distributions. Statistical Papers , 51 , 111–126. Petropoulos et al. [2022] Petropoulos, F., Apiletti, D., Assimakopoulos, V., Babai, M. Z., Barrow, D. K., Taieb, S. B., Bergmeir, C., Bessa, R. J., Bijak, J. et al. (2022). Forecasting: theory and practice. International Journal of Forecasting , 38 , 705–871. Pinson [2012] Pinson, P. (2012). Very-short-term probabilistic forecasting of wind power with generalized logit–normal distributions. Journal of the Royal Statistical Society: Series C (Applied Statistics) , 61 , 555–576. Ranjan &amp; Gneiting [2010] Ranjan, R., &amp; Gneiting, T. (2010). Combining probability forecasts. Journal of the Royal Statistical Society: Series B (Statistical Methodology) , 72 , 71–91. Spiekermann et al. [2015] Spiekermann, S., Acquisti, A., Böhme, R., &amp; Hui, K.-L. (2015). The challenges of personal data markets and privacy. Electronic Markets , 25 , 161–167. Winkler et al. [2019] Winkler, R. L., Grushka-Cockayne, Y., Lichtendahl Jr., K. C., &amp; Jose, V. R. R. (2019). Probability forecasts and their combination: A research perspective. Decision Analysis , 16 , 239–260. Winkler et al. [1996] Winkler, R. L., Muñoz, J., Cervera, J. L., Bernardo, J. M., Blattenberger, G., Kadane, J. B., Lindley, D. V., Murphy, A. H., Oliver, R. M., &amp; Ríos-Insua, D. (1996). Scoring rules and the evaluation of probabilities. Test , 5 , 1–60. Witkowski et al. [2018] Witkowski, J., Freeman, R., Vaughan, J., Pennock, D., &amp; Krause, A. (2018). Incentive-compatible forecasting competitions. In Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence . volume 32. Wolfers &amp; Zitzewitz [2006] Wolfers, J., &amp; Zitzewitz, E. (2006). Prediction markets in theor